  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**Please note that TLs are different for different subtasks.**\n\nMadoka decided to create her own chat with her friends in it. However, the chat was unmonitored for a while, so her friends started posting pictures of manuls with numbers in it. Coming back to the messy chat, Madoka knows that she cannot suspend it now, because that will make her friends hate her. Instead, she wants to understand the rules her friends are using to post manuls.\n\nMadoka and her friends all have the same favorite number KKK. After a little investigation, she realized that her friends are posting manuls using the following rules:\n\n\nInitially, a picture with only 111 manul is posted.\nIf the last picture posted has AAA manuls in it, then a picture with BBB manuls will be posted next if the following conditions are met:\n\nlcm(A,B)≤A⋅(A+1)\\textbf{lcm}(A, B) \\leq A \\cdot (A + 1)lcm(A,B)≤A⋅(A+1)\nA&lt;B≤A+KA \\lt B \\le A + KA&lt;B≤A+K\n\n\nMadoka knows that her friends will stop counting when a picture with at least NNN manuls is posted. Since this chat is hers, Madoka can suggest which picture to be posted each time. To not pollute the chat, Madoka is trying to find a sequence of pictures with the **minimum** number of pictures used.\n\nHelp Madoka!\n\n\nInput Format\nThe only line of input contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK.\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint the answer to the problem - the **minimum** number of pictures that can be used.",
    "constraints": [
      "3≤N≤10183 \\leq N \\leq 10^{18}3≤N≤1018",
      "3≤K≤1043 \\leq K \\leq 10^43≤K≤104",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 111 (20 points)**: 3≤K≤3003 \\leq K \\leq 3003≤K≤300, TL - 222 sec",
      "**Subtask 222 (40 points)**: 3≤K≤19003 \\leq K \\leq 19003≤K≤1900, TL - 888 sec",
      "**Subtask 333 (10 points)**: 3≤K≤30003 \\leq K \\leq 30003≤K≤3000, TL - 333 sec",
      "**Subtask 444 (30 points)**: Original constraints, TL - 333 sec"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4 3",
        "output": "3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nConsider the following sequence, where each element is the number of manuls in each picture: [1,2,4][1, 2, 4][1,2,4].\n\nFor the second picture with 222 manuls:\n\nlcm(1,2)=2≤1⋅(1+1)\\mathbf{lcm}(1, 2) = 2 \\le 1 \\cdot (1 + 1)lcm(1,2)=2≤1⋅(1+1)\n1<2≤1+31 \\lt 2 \\le 1 + 31<2≤1+3\n\n\nFor the third picture with 444 manuls:\n\nlcm(2,4)=4≤2⋅(2+1)\\mathbf{lcm}(2, 4) = 4 \\le 2 \\cdot (2 + 1)lcm(2,4)=4≤2⋅(2+1)\n2<4≤2+32 \\lt 4 \\le 2 + 32<4≤2+3\n\n\n\nNo shorter sequence of pictures is possible."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "29 7",
        "output": "7",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nOne of the shortest sequences of pictures is [1,2,6,12,18,24,30][1, 2, 6, 12, 18, 24, 30][1,2,6,12,18,24,30]."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "228 17",
        "output": "17",
        "explanation": ""
      }
    ]
  },
